# Demo Data Isolation

All files under `src/app/feature` outside the provider swap must be
**production-ready**. Demo/mock seed data lives under `src/demo/`, wired at
**provider level** — never in pages, config factories, or domain models.

## Allowed demo locations

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|-------|------|----------------|
| Demo seeds / fixtures | `src/demo/<domain>/<entity>/*-demo.fixtures.ts` (or `*.demo-data.ts`) | Pools, ref data, `DEMO_*` |
| Demo source | `src/demo/<domain>/<entity>/*-demo.data-source.ts` | Implements the port with demo data |
| Provider swap | `src/app/feature/.../data/*.providers.ts` | **Only** place that reads `MOCK_DATA` |

Mirror feature domain/entity paths under `src/demo/` (sibling of `src/app/`).

## Production files — never import demo

These must **not** import demo fixtures/sources, define `DEMO_*` constants, or
branch on `MOCK_DATA`:

- `page/`
- `config/`
- `domain/`
- `data/*-api.data-source.ts`, `data/*-data.mapper.ts`

Inject behavior through the **port** (`XDataSource`) instead.

Providers may import from `src/demo/...` solely for the `MOCK_DATA` swap.

## Provider pattern (single swap point)

```typescript
// data/<entity>.providers.ts — ONLY file that reads MOCK_DATA
import { EntityDemoDataSource } from 'src/demo/<domain>/<entity>/<entity>-demo.data-source';

export function provideEntityInfrastructure(): Provider[] {
  if (MOCK_DATA) {
    return [EntityDemoDataSource, { provide: EntityDataSource, useExisting: EntityDemoDataSource }];
  }
  return [EntityApiDataSource, { provide: EntityDataSource, useExisting: EntityApiDataSource }];
}
```

## Not demo data (allowed in production)

Production **fallbacks** for missing backend reference data are acceptable —
defensive defaults, not seed records.

## Scan checklist

```bash
rg "from ['\"]src/demo|DEMO_|MOCK_DATA" src/app/feature/<entity>/ \
  --glob '!**/*.providers.ts'
```
